TH to each of them for fees.\n\n| # | Quote | Action | In | Out (est.) | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | q_1 | Swap ETH → WBTC on Ethereum | 0.1 ETH | 495000 WBTC base units | $3.90 |\n| 2 | q_2 | Send ETH for fees, Ethereum → Robinhood | 0.001 ETH | 833333333333333 wei | $1.40 |\n| 3 | q_3 | Send ETH for fees, Ethereum → Arbitrum | 0.001 ETH | 833333333333333 wei | $1.40 |\n| 4 | q_4 | Send WBTC, Ethereum → Robinhood | 247500 | 246666 | $1.40 |\n| 5 | q_5 | Send WBTC, Ethereum → Arbitrum | 247500 | 246666 | $1.40 |\n| 6 | q_7 | Swap WBTC → ETH on Robinhood | 246666 | 49233200000000000 wei (~0.0492 ETH) | $0.36 |\n| 7 | q_8 | Swap WBTC → USDC on Arbitrum | 246666 | 147699600 (~147.70 USDC) | $0.36 |\n\n**Expected balances after the route:**\n- **Ethereum:** about 0.0465 ETH and 0 WBTC.\n- **Robinhood Chain:** about 0.0500 ETH (the swap output plus what's left of the fee ETH).\n- **Arbitrum:** about 147.70 USDC and about 0.00081 ETH left for future fees.\n\nI picked this route because it was the cheapest one I priced. The other way to get USDC is to swap on Ethereum and then send the USDC to Arbitrum. That costs about $3.90 more, and the Arbitrum wallet would still need ETH for fees.\n\n**Timing:** each transfer between networks takes about 60 seconds. I'll run the steps one at a time and check the balance after each. These quotes expire after 300 seconds, so I may need to get fresh prices when we start.\n\nReply **approve** to run it, or tell me a lower cost limit."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":22,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":23,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_9"},"id":"toolu_014dhr2VnUB4t7APuxV8sMh7"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":24,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_10\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_014dhr2VnUB4t7APuxV8sMh7","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","isEr